summary:
  Any device the record is asked about may be sent a level: one that
  refused the stream and one still being asked among them.

history:
  Every ticked device was sent the widget's level, with every move of the
  slider and every mute. A device that refuses the stream stays ticked,
  and it has a life of its own: a Ruark that had refused stood beside a
  television that played, and its level went from 10 to 6 during a test
  whose commands never named it (2026-11-12). It may have been playing
  its own radio. A level goes only to a device that answered it plays.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CastLogic.js

find:
      return typeof uuid === "string" && _copy(session).on[uuid] === true;

replace:
      return typeof uuid === "string";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_castlogic.qml::test_only_a_device_that_plays_is_sent_a_level.
